  "title": "Bolo Rei",
  "subtitle": "Portuguese Christmas king's bread with dried fruits and nuts",
  "excerpt": "Bolo Rei is the Portuguese Christmas bread eaten on the Feast of the Epiphany (6 January), shaped like a crown, fragrant with orange blossom water and lemon zest, and studded with dried fruits and chopped nuts. The dough is enriched with egg, butter, and a little port, which makes it soft and slightly cake-like rather than bready. A whole dried fava bean is traditionally hidden inside; whoever finds it in their slice must buy next year's cake.",
