  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Bolo Rei (king's bread) is a Portuguese festive bread with French origins: it derives from the galette des rois tradition and arrived in Portugal in the 19th century via the Confeitaria Nacional in Lisbon, which sold the first Bolo Rei in 1869. The recipe is documented in Portuguese cookery books from the late 19th century onward and is now the standard Epiphany cake throughout Portugal and the Portuguese diaspora.",
