      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mix and knead the dough"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Combine {{plain-flour}}, {{yeast-fast-action}}, {{sea-salt-fine}}, and {{caster-sugar}} in a large bowl. Add {{eggs}}, {{whole-milk}}, {{orange-blossom-water}}, and the zest of {{lemon}}. Mix to a rough dough, then turn out and knead for 8 minutes until smooth and elastic. Add {{unsalted-butter}} a little at a time, kneading it in fully before the next addition; this takes about 10 minutes by hand or 6 minutes in a stand mixer on medium speed. The finished dough should be soft, slightly tacky, and pass the windowpane test: a small piece stretched gently should stretch thin without tearing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bulk ferment"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Place the dough in a lightly oiled bowl, cover with cling film, and leave at room temperature for 1 hour 30 minutes until doubled in size. The enrichment slows fermentation; in a cool kitchen it may take up to 2 hours."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Add the fruit and shape"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Turn the risen dough out and flatten gently. Scatter {{sultanas}}, {{mixed-peel}}, and {{walnuts}} over the surface and fold the dough over and around them. Knead briefly to distribute evenly. Form into a ball, then use your thumbs to push a hole through the centre. Gradually stretch the ring to about 24 cm in diameter and place on a lined baking tray. Cover loosely with oiled cling film and prove for 1 hour until noticeably puffed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Glaze and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 180°C (conventional). Brush the ring generously with beaten egg wash. Bake for 25 to 30 minutes until deep golden brown and the loaf sounds hollow when tapped on the underside. Cover loosely with foil after 15 minutes if the surface is colouring too quickly. Cool on a wire rack for at least 20 minutes. Dust with {{icing-sugar}} just before serving."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
